<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR mostly lower on excess liquidity.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR mostly lower on excess liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly lower due to excess peso liquidity in the market, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The PHIBOR is just tracking the overnight and term rates,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Most of the maturities slipped marginally, except for the one-week, two-week and one-year maturities which remained constant from yesterday's level.</p>
<p>PHIBOR are average swap rates quoted by 20 banks operating in the country.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 APR 24		  APR 23</p>
<p>    1 W		9 11/16		 9 11/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9 11/16		 9 11/16</p>
<p>    1 M		9 11/16		 9  3/4</p>
<p>    2 M		9  3/4		  9 13/16</p>
<p>    3 M		9  7/8		  9 15/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  1/8		 10  3/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  3/8		 10  3/8</p>
<p>    VAL		25-Apr		  24-Apr</p>
